{
  "title": "Fail test orchestration when stale services occupy test ports",
  "description": "A timed-out `make test` left the fixture server, mock \
OpenRouter, and API server running as orphaned processes. A later `make test` \
logged address-in-use failures when its replacement services tried to bind, \
but the API tests connected to the stale services and the overall target \
exited successfully. This can produce a false green result against binaries or \
fixtures from an earlier run.\n\
\n\
The test harness should reliably terminate its full process tree on \
interruption and must fail fast when any required service process fails to \
start, even if a health check can reach an unrelated process already listening \
on the configured port. Add a regression test covering stale listeners and \
externally terminated orchestration.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 1,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "testing",
    "tooling",
  ],
